.\" Man page for snifdog, the SNIF CA Transparency watchdog.
.\" Keep in sync with the usage() text in snifdog/bin/snifdog, snifdog/README,
.\" and snifdog/DESIGN.md.  Version: $VERSION in bin/snifdog.
.TH SNIFDOG 8 "2026-07-05" "snifdog 0.1" "SNIF Manual"
.SH NAME
snifdog \- SNIF Certificate Transparency watchdog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snifdog pin
.I name
.RB [ \-\-from
.IR cert " | " \-\-spki
.IR hex ]
.RB [ \-\-issuer
.IR s ]
.br
.B snifdog poll
.br
.B snifdog watch
.br
.B snifdog list
.br
.B snifdog help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snifdog
monitors public Certificate Transparency (CT) logs for certificates issued under
a SNIF namespace and alerts on any certificate for a SNIF name whose
SubjectPublicKeyInfo (SPKI) is not the key the legitimate device holds. It turns
SNIF security\-model guarantee #3 \(em that relay or CA misbehavior is publicly
detectable via CT \(em from a claim into a running detector.
.PP
Because SNIF binds one key to one name for life (a device never re\-keys; a new
key gets a new
.I snif\-xxxx
name), a name's SPKI is immutable. snifdog pins the SHA\-256 of the DER SPKI (the
RFC 7469 construction): a legitimate renewal (same key, new serial) is silent,
while a key\-substitution impersonation fires immediately. There is no rotation
false\-positive class.
.PP
Run co\-located with the SNIF CA proxy (its
.I csr/
store present), snifdog additionally validates each certificate against the one
CSR the proxy keyed for the name \(em proven ground truth, per name \(em rather
than trusting the first cert seen.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "pin " name " " [options]
Anchor a name's SPKI explicitly \(em the strongest anchor, needing no relay, CA,
or first\-use trust.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-from " cert"
Read the SPKI from a certificate file (PEM or DER). If
.I name
is omitted it is taken from the certificate's SANs. Defaults to the local
connector certificate when neither
.B \-\-from
nor
.B \-\-spki
is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-spki " hex"
Pin a SHA\-256 SPKI hash directly, as 64 hex characters.
.TP
.BI \-\-issuer " s"
Record an expected issuer string with the pin.
.RE
.TP
.B poll
One incremental CT pass, intended for cron. Exits
.B 2
if a new alert was raised this pass.
.TP
.B watch
Long\-running loop; polls every
.I SNIFDOG_POLL_INTERVAL
seconds.
.TP
.B list
Print the pin database.
.TP
.B help
Print a usage summary.
.SH MODES
The run mode is set by
.I SNIFDOG_MODE
in the configuration:
.TP
.B watch
Independent watcher (default). Alerts on any observed SPKI outside the pin set;
needs no access to relay or CA\-proxy data, so a device owner or a third party can
run it. This is the configuration that actually delivers guarantee #3.
.TP
.B reconcile
Operator enrichment, co\-located with the CA proxy: cross\-checks observations
against the CA\-proxy CSR set to auto\-classify the operator's own reissues.
.TP
.B both
Watch semantics enriched with the CSR\-set cross\-check.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No alert.
.TP
.B 2
.RB ( poll )
A new alert was raised this pass.
.TP
.B 75
.RB ( pin ", " watch )
Another snifdog process holds the state directory.
.B poll
skips instead, exiting 0.
.TP
.B 78
The state directory belongs to another base domain, or holds pins outside
this one.
.TP
.B non\-zero
A fetch or configuration error occurred.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I SNIFDOG_CONF
Path to the configuration file (default
.IR /etc/snif/snifdog.conf ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/snif/snifdog.conf
Configuration: namespace, CT source, mode, alert sinks. One configuration
watches one base domain.
.TP
.I /etc/snif/snifdog.d/*.conf
One configuration per base domain. The cron entry runs a pass for each, and
for
.I /etc/snif/snifdog.conf
if it exists; in watch mode, run one
.BI snifdog@ base .service
per file. Each defaults its state directory to
.IR /var/lib/snif/snifdog/ base ,
since two bases must never share one.
.TP
.I /etc/snif/snif.conf
SNIF relay configuration, sourced for
.IR SNIF_CA_PROXY .
.TP
.I /var/lib/snif/snifdog/pins/
One SPKI pin record per watched name.
.TP
.I /var/lib/snif/snifdog/var/
Per\-source cursor and the already\-alerted cache; the owning base domain
.RI ( base )
and the lock each pass holds
.RI ( lock ).
.TP
.I /var/lib/snif/snifdog/evidence/
Per\-detection evidence bundles.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snifd (8),
.BR snif\-conn (1)
.PP
